infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Head vs tail sampling: where the keep-or-drop decision is made
  desc Both cut trace volume — only one keeps the rare slow and failing requests
  compares
    - label Head sampling
      children
        - label Decides at the root
          desc Before the request runs, blind to how it ends
        - label Keeps 10% by ratio
          desc TraceIdRatioBasedSampler(0.1) — cheap, no extra infrastructure
        - label Misses rare slow and failing requests
          desc A low rate drops the exact traces you added tracing to find
    - label Tail sampling
      children
        - label Decides after the request finishes
          desc Outcome known — keep all errors and all slow traces
        - label Catches the rare bad request
          desc Samples only a small fraction of boring fast successes
        - label Needs the OpenTelemetry Collector
          desc Buffers every span until the trace completes to judge it
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
